"""Outbound-webhooks tests — requires the `db`, `users`, and `worker` extras.

NO live infrastructure: the relay is driven with a fake ``enqueue_fn`` (no Redis) and every
outbound HTTP call is mocked with respx (no network). Proves the contract end to end — endpoint
CRUD, that ``dispatch`` writes ONE pending row to the transactional outbox, that the relay
publishes it (one signed delivery per subscribed endpoint), is replay-safe, and dead-letters a
permanently-unqueuable event, and that the worker task POSTs with a correct HMAC-SHA256 signature
and retries on failure. Runs against the throwaway SQLite database from `conftest.pytest_configure`.
"""

